Relevant columns & their potential usage  

• THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.ORDER_ITEMS  
  – "product_id": join‑key to product data  
  – "inventory_item_id": join‑key to get unit cost from INVENTORY_ITEMS  
  – "sale_price": revenue portion of profit calculation  
  – "status": let us ignore rows with ‘Cancelled’ or ‘Returned’ (and any other non‑sale status)  
  – "returned_at": if NOT NULL the item was returned → must be excluded  
  – "created_at": micro‑seconds timestamp used to group rows by month  

• THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.INVENTORY_ITEMS  
  – "id": join‑key from ORDER_ITEMS."inventory_item_id"  
  – "cost": unit cost portion of profit calculation  
  – "product_name": human‑friendly name of the SKU (optional)  
  – "product_id": alternative join‑key to PRODUCTS if needed  
  – "sold_at": timestamp that can be used instead of ORDER_ITEMS."created_at" when we only care about items actually sold  

• THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.PRODUCTS  
  – "id": join‑key from ORDER_ITEMS."product_id" or INVENTORY_ITEMS."product_id"  
  – "name": formal product name we finally want to list  
  – "category", "department", "brand": extra description fields (optional)  

Conditions that will probably be used later  
1. Exclude cancelled items → "status" NOT ILIKE '%cancel%'  
2. Exclude returned items → "returned_at" IS NULL  
3. Restrict date range → "created_at" between Jan‑2019 and Aug‑2022 (when converted to dates)  


